index 0000000..9743582
--- /dev/null
+++ b/THRESHOLD_FEATURE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@
+# Threshold Feature Implementation
+
+## Overview
+Implemented `--threshold` option for `frai eval` command to gate CI jobs on evaluation metrics.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. frai-core (SDK)
+**File: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`**
+- Added `validateThresholds(thresholds, evaluations)` function
+  - Validates threshold format (metric id exists, value is 0-1)
+  - Returns `{ valid: boolean, errors: string[] }`
+  - Lists all valid metric ids in error messages for unknown metrics
+  
+- Added `evaluateThresholds(thresholds, evaluations)` function
+  - Evaluates each threshold against metric scores
+  - Returns array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` for each threshold
+  - Handles null scores (counts as failed)
+
+- Modified `generateReport()` function
+  - Accepts optional `thresholds` parameter
+  - Adds `passed` field to report when thresholds provided
+  - Adds `thresholds` array to report with pass/fail details
+  - Only includes these fields when thresholds are provided and non-empty
+
+- Exported both new functions (named and default exports)
+
+**File: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`**
+- Updated `toMarkdown()` function
+  - Adds "## Thresholds" section to markdown reports
+  - Shows PASS/FAIL status, score, and minimum for each threshold
+  - Only includes section when thresholds are present
+
+**File: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`**
+- Added tests for new threshold functionality
+
+**File: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/thresholds.test.js`**
+- Created comprehensive test suite for threshold validation and evaluation
+
+### 2. frai-cli (CLI)
+**File: `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**
+- Updated `EvalOptions` interface
+  - Added `threshold?: string[]` field
+  
+- Added `parseThreshold(str)` helper function
+  - Parses "metric=value" format
+  - Validates value is between 0 and 1
+  - Throws on malformed input
+
+- Added `parseThresholds(strs)` helper function
+  - Converts array of threshold strings to `{ metric: value }` object
+  
+- Modified `runEvalCommand()` function
+  - Parses thresholds from CLI options
+  - Validates thresholds using `Eval.validateThresholds()`
+  - Exits with code 2 on validation errors (malformed threshold or unknown metric)
+  - Passes validated thresholds to `generateReport()`
+  - Exits with code 1 if `report.passed === false`
+  - Exits with code 0 if all thresholds pass or no thresholds provided
+  
+- Updated eval command definition
+  - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option
+  - Option can be specified multiple times
+  - Help text explains the behavior
+
+### 3. Documentation
+**File: `packages/frai-core/README.md`**
+- Updated `frai eval` command documentation
+  - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option description
+  - Explains exit codes (0 success, 1 threshold failure, 2 validation error)
+  
+- Added "Eval with Thresholds" section in SDK examples
+  - Shows how to use `validateThresholds()` and `generateReport()` with thresholds
+  - Demonstrates proper error handling and exit codes
+
+## Behavior
+
+### CLI Usage
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95
+
+# Without thresholds (unchanged behavior)
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json
+```
+
+### Exit Codes
+- **0**: Success (all thresholds passed or no thresholds specified)
+- **1**: Threshold validation failed (at least one metric didn't meet minimum)
+- **2**: Invalid usage (malformed threshold or unknown metric id)
+
+### Report Format
+
+**JSON**: Report includes `passed` and `thresholds` fields when thresholds are used:
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ],
+  "passed": true,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 1.0,
+      "passed": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+**Markdown**: Report includes "## Thresholds" section:
+```
+## Thresholds
+
+- **exact_match:** PASS (score: 1.0, min: 0.9)
+```
+
+## Edge Cases Handled
+- Metric with null score fails threshold
+- Unknown metric id lists all valid metric ids in error
+- Threshold value outside 0-1 range rejected
+- Multiple same thresholds (last one wins)
+- Empty thresholds object treated as no thresholds
+- Reports without thresholds unchanged from before
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+- No breaking changes
+- Existing reports without thresholds unchanged
+- All existing metrics supported (exact_match, toxicity, length_variance)
+- Custom metrics supported (if passed to runEvaluations)
